3
00:00:29.007 --> 00:00:30.300
My name is Kevin Porter.

4
00:00:30.926 --> 00:00:33.345
I'm a guidance counselor
at Liberty High School.

5
00:00:37.933 --> 00:00:40.269
I would say I help as
many kids as I can.

6
00:00:42.396 --> 00:00:44.106
That's why I got into education.

7
00:00:45.941 --> 00:00:47.985
But I don't get to see every kid.

8
00:00:49.695 --> 00:00:51.196
I try to keep an eye out.

9
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.740
but you have to count
on kids to come to you.

10
00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.839
And not every kid who does come to you

11
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.360
is able to ask for the help they need.

12
00:01:01.832 --> 00:01:04.167
Not every kid tells you the whole truth.

13
00:01:08.005 --> 00:01:09.506
We all need it.

14
00:01:10.173 --> 00:01:11.216
Human contact.

15
00:01:11.758 --> 00:01:15.804
And communications class. crazy as
it was. was human contact for me.

16
00:01:16.888 --> 00:01:19.182
Until someone in that
class cut my lifeline.

17
00:01:19.725 --> 00:01:21.602
Someone who was known for being sweet.

18
00:01:22.561 --> 00:01:25.355
I'll tell you who it is. but
you're going to have to wait.

19
00:01:26.523 --> 00:01:27.649
- Just like I did.
- Hey.

20
00:01:27.733 --> 00:01:28.733
Oh!

21
00:01:29.651 --> 00:01:30.651
Kevin.

22
00:01:30.777 --> 00:01:33.238
Uh. what are you doing here on a Sunday?

23
00:01:33.322 --> 00:01:35.282
I should be asking you
the same question.

24
00:01:35.699 --> 00:01:37.659
I thought I'd have the place to myself.

25
00:01:38.035 --> 00:01:40.412
Well. they bumped me up.

26
00:01:40.579 --> 00:01:42.372
I testify first thing in the morning.

27
00:01:42.456 --> 00:01:44.124
Wow. Me. too.

28
00:01:44.666 --> 00:01:46.293
So. I guess I go after you?

29
00:01:46.376 --> 00:01:47.376
Oh.

30
00:01:47.836 --> 00:01:49.129
So. what's this about?

31
00:01:51.673 --> 00:01:53.800
I couldn't listen when
they first came out.

32
00:01:54.718 --> 00:01:55.886
But now I just...

33
00:01:57.804 --> 00:01:58.972
can't stop listening.

34
00:01:59.806 --> 00:02:00.806
Ah.

35
00:02:02.225 --> 00:02:04.269
- So you're here preparing?
- Yeah.

36
00:02:05.687 --> 00:02:06.767
Isn't that why you're here?

37
00:02:07.898 --> 00:02:10.901
I sat down. you know. with the
lawyers. I know what to say.

38
00:02:11.443 --> 00:02:12.986
We followed protocol.

39
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:16.740
We did all we could for Hannah
with the information that we had.

40
00:02:17.866 --> 00:02:21.953
I sat down with them. too.
and I feel like it's true.

41
00:02:26.041 --> 00:02:30.212
Well... but the world is not listening
to a recording of your class.

42
00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.508
They're not gonna play the
tape in court. though.

43
00:02:35.676 --> 00:02:36.885
That's what the lawyers say.

44
00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.014
But they know what's on it.
and they know what happened.

45
00:02:42.265 --> 00:02:43.705
But you know what was in your heart.

46
00:02:44.685 --> 00:02:46.205
She couldn't tell you what she needed.

47
00:02:46.728 --> 00:02:47.771
You did your best.

48
00:02:49.815 --> 00:02:50.815
Did I?

49
00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:10.119
Not every kid who comes to you in pain

50
00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:12.280
can tell you where it hurts.

51
00:03:12.421 --> 00:03:13.755
I need it to stop.

52
00:03:15.048 --> 00:03:16.508
You need what to stop?

53
00:03:17.426 --> 00:03:20.262
I need everything to stop.

54
00:03:21.972 --> 00:03:25.225
Just. people. life.

55
00:03:26.226 --> 00:03:29.479
What did you mean when you
said you needed life to stop?

56
00:03:30.021 --> 00:03:31.021
I don't know.

57
00:03:31.398 --> 00:03:34.151
'Cause that seems like a
very serious thing to say.

58
00:03:34.526 --> 00:03:35.526
I know. I...

59
00:03:36.236 --> 00:03:38.780
I'm sorry. I didn't mean... that.

60
00:03:41.408 --> 00:03:43.076
She said she didn't mean it.

61
00:03:44.035 --> 00:03:45.954
I made the mistake of believing her.

62
00:03:51.793 --> 00:03:53.879
Hannah told me she was struggling.

63
00:03:53.962 --> 00:03:56.506
but she didn't specifically
mention suicide.

64
00:03:56.590 --> 00:03:58.190
I just need everything to stop.

65
00:03:58.633 --> 00:04:00.218
What do you need to stop. Hannah?

66
00:04:00.802 --> 00:04:02.804
Do I really need to
spell it out for you?

67
00:04:04.723 --> 00:04:06.725
I'm thinking about killing myself.

68
00:04:07.809 --> 00:04:09.603
If she had said those words.

69
00:04:10.103 --> 00:04:11.897
of course I would have taken action.

70
00:04:12.105 --> 00:04:14.566
Did you have an encounter at the party?

71
00:04:15.942 --> 00:04:16.943
An encounter?

72
00:04:18.987 --> 00:04:21.448
Yeah. You could say that.

73
00:04:21.531 --> 00:04:23.158
Did he force himself on you?

74
00:04:24.826 --> 00:04:25.826
I think so.

75
00:04:25.994 --> 00:04:28.246
You think so. but you're not sure?

76
00:04:29.873 --> 00:04:31.374
Did you tell him to stop?

77
00:04:32.918 --> 00:04:33.918
No.

78
00:04:34.169 --> 00:04:35.253
Did you tell him "no"?

79
00:04:38.465 --> 00:04:39.465
No.

80
00:04:40.008 --> 00:04:41.768
Maybe you consented.
then changed your mind.

81
00:04:41.802 --> 00:04:43.220
No. it's not like that.

82
00:04:45.013 --> 00:04:47.140
Should we involve your
parents or the police?

83
00:04:47.224 --> 00:04:48.224
No!

84
00:04:51.186 --> 00:04:52.354
Hannah. who's the boy?

85
00:04:56.316 --> 00:04:59.194
I think we all wish it could
have gone differently.

86
00:05:00.487 --> 00:05:01.488
What happened. Hannah?

87
00:05:03.907 --> 00:05:06.368
I got into a hot tub
with Bryce Walker...

88
00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.500
and then he raped me.

89
00:05:18.713 --> 00:05:22.008
We can have the best intentions
and still fall short.

90
00:05:31.309 --> 00:05:34.354
No Justin this morning? He's
usually the first one up.

91
00:05:35.272 --> 00:05:36.272
He's...

92
00:05:37.065 --> 00:05:38.316
not our problem anymore.

93
00:05:39.776 --> 00:05:41.820
What does that mean.
he's not our problem?

94
00:05:45.115 --> 00:05:46.575
It means he's gone.

95
00:05:48.243 --> 00:05:49.243
He took off.

96
00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:53.290
- Did you try calling him?
- He doesn't have a phone.

97
00:05:53.832 --> 00:05:55.959
Your mother gave him one
on the family plan.

98
00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:59.838
- Of course she did.
- Well. we should call him.

99
00:06:01.256 --> 00:06:04.217
I don't know his number. I imagine
the phone company will have it.

100
00:06:04.301 --> 00:06:05.302
Jesus. why do you care?

101
00:06:05.969 --> 00:06:07.262
He had a bed. he had food.

102
00:06:07.345 --> 00:06:10.181
he had new clothes. and a
new phone. apparently.

103
00:06:10.432 --> 00:06:11.725
and he didn't want any of it.

104
00:06:12.309 --> 00:06:14.936
- So why don't we just let him go?
- Clay. what's this about?

105
00:06:16.104 --> 00:06:17.564
He's scheduled to testify on Monday.

106
00:06:17.647 --> 00:06:20.001
and that was so important to
you. you smuggled him in here.

107
00:06:20.025 --> 00:06:21.109
Where's Mom?

108
00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:26.448
Your mother and I had a...
disagreement last night.

109
00:06:26.531 --> 00:06:27.616
Yeah. I was there.

110
00:06:27.699 --> 00:06:30.952
And she's staying with her
sister for a few days.

111
00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:31.960
Why?

112
00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.831
Oh. just to give us both
time to figure things out.

113
00:06:36.082 --> 00:06:39.044
The past few weeks have been
stressful around here for all of us.

114
00:06:39.419 --> 00:06:40.420
Let's move.

115
00:06:41.755 --> 00:06:43.840
Start over somewhere. just you and me.

116
00:06:44.257 --> 00:06:46.301
Clay. it's... It's not permanent.

117
00:06:46.384 --> 00:06:49.429
- Your mom and I are just cooling off.
- I don't care. I don't...

118
00:06:50.889 --> 00:06:52.682
ever wanna go to that school again.

119
00:06:54.059 --> 00:06:55.299
Look. everybody hates me there.

120
00:06:55.477 --> 00:06:58.355
Someone online called me a murderer
because I was on Hannah's tapes.

121
00:06:58.647 --> 00:07:01.858
Why do you read what people say online?

122
00:07:02.609 --> 00:07:03.652
Let's move.

123
00:07:04.569 --> 00:07:05.820
- Anywhere.
- Clay.

124
00:07:07.322 --> 00:07:10.033
This is our home. All right?
This is our family.

125
00:07:11.076 --> 00:07:12.285
We've made a bit of a mess.

126
00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.163
But nothing's broken we can't fix.

127
00:07:16.247 --> 00:07:17.247
Everything's broken.

128
00:07:20.293 --> 00:07:22.170
And I don't think any
of it can be fixed.

129
00:07:24.756 --> 00:07:26.716
Some kids can't speak their truth.

130
00:07:27.509 --> 00:07:28.509
Some won't.

131
00:07:28.927 --> 00:07:31.262
To us. to their families...

132
00:07:33.014 --> 00:07:34.265
We can go ahead and eat.

133
00:07:34.766 --> 00:07:38.269
It's Sunday morning. There's no
hurry. We'll wait for our guest.

134
00:07:38.353 --> 00:07:41.106
She said 10:00 was fine. so I
don't know what's going on.

135
00:07:42.732 --> 00:07:45.735
Was this before or after the
ribbon cutting ceremony?

136
00:07:46.152 --> 00:07:48.989
I mean. I invited her
yesterday at school.

137
00:07:49.072 --> 00:07:51.366
And did she confirm? She
might not know to confirm.

138
00:07:51.820 --> 00:07:53.439
Not everyone has a grandmother like

139
00:07:53.440 --> 00:07:55.720
yours. wielding Emily Post like a bible.

140
00:07:56.037 --> 00:07:59.290
- She knows things like that.
- Well. then. I wonder what's keeping her.

141
00:08:01.209 --> 00:08:04.546
Did the two of you discuss
the ceremony at all?

142
00:08:04.629 --> 00:08:06.339
No. Chlöe doesn't care about that stuff.

143
00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:10.260
I'll just... I'm gonna try her again.

144
00:08:15.306 --> 00:08:16.641
What are you doing?

145
00:08:18.393 --> 00:08:20.705
- I don't know what you mean.
- You know exactly what I mean.

146
00:08:20.729 --> 00:08:21.813
Leave the boy alone.

147
00:08:22.856 --> 00:08:25.775
Can you honestly say you recognize
the person on that tape?

148
00:08:26.735 --> 00:08:29.946
Have you ever said anything even
remotely resembling the filth

149
00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.322
that came out of his mouth?

150
00:08:31.406 --> 00:08:33.450
It was a setup. He was drunk.

151
00:08:33.825 --> 00:08:35.243
That was not our son talking.

152
00:08:35.326 --> 00:08:37.954
You're his mother. for Christ's
sake. You raised him.

153
00:08:41.916 --> 00:08:44.961
She's still not picking up.
Let's just eat. I guess.

154
00:08:46.004 --> 00:08:47.004
Marisa?

155
00:08:47.797 --> 00:08:48.923
If you would. please.

156
00:08:53.595 --> 00:08:56.681
Son. if something's not right with
Chlöe. you need to make it right.

157
00:08:58.308 --> 00:08:59.308
Do you understand?

158
00:09:01.311 --> 00:09:02.437
Yeah. Dad.

159
00:09:02.687 --> 00:09:06.024
A woman who loves you is to be respected

160
00:09:07.025 --> 00:09:08.151
and not to be crossed.

161
00:09:16.743 --> 00:09:19.704
And some kids have secrets
they believe they have to keep

162
00:09:20.622 --> 00:09:21.915
for their own survival.

163
00:09:24.209 --> 00:09:26.252
You can't hide in this
town with that car.

164
00:09:27.087 --> 00:09:29.089
- Hey.
- Hey? That's what I get?

165
00:09:29.631 --> 00:09:31.271
You're sitting when
you should be boxing.

166
00:09:31.549 --> 00:09:33.986
I can't always find someone to fill
a Saturday session last-minute.

167
00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:36.096
Yeah. I'm sorry. okay?
There's a lot going on.

168
00:09:37.472 --> 00:09:38.598
Yeah. Yeah. clearly.

169
00:09:39.265 --> 00:09:40.475
You wanna tell me about Lucas?

170
00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:43.937
- Who?
- Lucas.

171
00:09:44.145 --> 00:09:46.773
You met him last night. you got
weird. and then you bailed.

172
00:09:46.856 --> 00:09:48.140
Then this morning. you didn't show up.

173
00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.300
It's got nothing to do with Lucas. okay?

174
00:09:50.318 --> 00:09:51.402
It's the trial.

175
00:09:51.653 --> 00:09:53.113
And now these tapes.

176
00:09:53.320 --> 00:09:54.322
Yeah. that's some shit.

177
00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:57.439
And I've never lost a
friend like that. but

178
00:09:57.440 --> 00:09:59.020
if you wanna talk about it...

179
00:10:01.037 --> 00:10:05.375
I'm not going to be right
until after I testify.

180
00:10:06.084 --> 00:10:07.877
And I shouldn't have left you hanging.

181
00:10:07.961 --> 00:10:10.672
I didn't want to make my drama yours.

182
00:10:10.964 --> 00:10:11.964
And...

183
00:10:13.883 --> 00:10:14.883
I'm sorry.

184
00:10:15.885 --> 00:10:17.137
Now. was that so hard?

185
00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:20.974
Oh. fuck you. Yes. actually. Yes.

186
00:10:21.558 --> 00:10:22.809
Wanna take your mind off it all

187
00:10:22.892 --> 00:10:24.812
and watch Madrid destroy
Barcelona Monday night?

188
00:10:25.687 --> 00:10:27.438
What makes you think I like soccer?

189
00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:30.170
You're Mexican and you're gay.
How could you not like soccer?

190
00:10:32.235 --> 00:10:33.778
Yeah. okay.

191
00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.530
It's a date.

192
00:10:39.033 --> 00:10:41.452
And we may think we know
what they're going through.

193
00:10:42.662 --> 00:10:44.164
but each kid goes through it...

194
00:10:45.957 --> 00:10:47.125
in their own way.

195
00:10:47.208 --> 00:10:49.878
Hi. Um. can I please have a large Coke

196
00:10:50.128 --> 00:10:53.965
and a medium popcorn. uh.
with butter only on half?

197
00:10:54.799 --> 00:10:56.551
But not the bottom half.

198
00:10:56.634 --> 00:10:58.595
Like. fill it up normally

199
00:10:58.678 --> 00:11:01.472
and then carefully put butter
only on the left half.

200
00:11:03.933 --> 00:11:07.103
It's very important. Just half.

201
00:11:10.148 --> 00:11:11.468
I'll have the same thing. please.

202
00:12:20.259 --> 00:12:21.302
What's wrong?

203
00:12:22.637 --> 00:12:24.389
- Sorry. bathroom.
- Wait. Tyler.

204
00:12:33.856 --> 00:12:35.149
Oh. fuck!

205
00:12:35.608 --> 00:12:36.608
Oh. shit.

206
00:12:37.026 --> 00:12:39.779
And so they think they're
the only person in the world

207
00:12:39.860 --> 00:12:41.459
feeling what they're feeling.

208
00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:43.980
and that no one could
possibly understand.

209
00:12:57.755 --> 00:12:59.007
Advance!

210
00:13:01.134 --> 00:13:02.134
On your left!

211
00:13:02.550 --> 00:13:03.553
Go. go!

212
00:13:05.138 --> 00:13:06.138
Go. go!

213
00:13:06.806 --> 00:13:07.806
Reload!

214
00:13:08.808 --> 00:13:10.408
Grenade!

215
00:13:11.394 --> 00:13:12.812
Move on. move on.

216
00:13:19.027 --> 00:13:22.530
They think that what's
hurting can never be healed.

217
00:13:27.076 --> 00:13:28.619
So they don't tell us.

218
00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:30.705
They hide. they deflect.

219
00:13:31.414 --> 00:13:34.125
They try to become the person
they think we want to see.

220
00:13:40.548 --> 00:13:43.134
Hey. baby. You want some lunch?

221
00:13:44.427 --> 00:13:45.511
Isn't it. like. 10:00?

222
00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.555
Uh. dinner. then?

223
00:13:47.638 --> 00:13:49.390
I can... I can make you something.

224
00:13:50.808 --> 00:13:52.518
Yeah. well. there's
hardly anything left.

225
00:13:52.602 --> 00:13:54.922
We ate most of the groceries yesterday.

226
00:13:55.688 --> 00:13:58.107
I forgot how much a growing boy can eat.

227
00:13:59.317 --> 00:14:04.280
Yeah. There's also only so many
actual groceries at 7-Eleven.

228
00:14:04.363 --> 00:14:05.406
Look at you.

229
00:14:06.657 --> 00:14:07.700
You're taller.

230
00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:09.910
I'm not.

231
00:14:10.995 --> 00:14:12.997
I basically shrunk on the streets.

232
00:14:13.456 --> 00:14:17.085
Well. you're still my
big. tall. handsome boy.

233
00:14:19.295 --> 00:14:20.295
I missed you.

234
00:14:22.632 --> 00:14:23.716
I missed you. too. Mom.

235
00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:30.500
It's... It's nothing.

236
00:14:30.515 --> 00:14:33.601
What'd you get into out there? I
never wanted this life for you.

237
00:14:33.684 --> 00:14:35.728
- I know.
- You don't deserve that life.

238
00:14:35.812 --> 00:14:36.812
Nobody does.

239
00:14:37.105 --> 00:14:38.773
Then why are you still with Seth?

240
00:14:39.565 --> 00:14:40.900
Baby...

241
00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:43.610
He loves me.

242
00:14:44.195 --> 00:14:47.824
Come on. okay? We can find a new place.

243
00:14:47.907 --> 00:14:49.951
We... We can get the fuck out of here.

244
00:14:51.119 --> 00:14:52.745
I can't. baby. you know that.

245
00:14:54.288 --> 00:14:55.540
And I need you here.

246
00:14:57.250 --> 00:14:59.377
Promise me you'll stay this time.

247
00:15:01.504 --> 00:15:02.504
Yeah. yeah.

248
00:15:04.132 --> 00:15:05.132
I promise.

249
00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:11.639
If you don't want to press charges

250
00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:13.265
against this boy.

251
00:15:13.266 --> 00:15:15.601
if you're not even sure
you can press charges.

252
00:15:16.853 --> 00:15:19.772
then there really is only one option.

253
00:15:20.898 --> 00:15:22.218
What is it?

254
00:15:23.401 --> 00:15:26.988
I'm not trying to be blunt here.
Hannah. but you can move on.

255
00:15:48.843 --> 00:15:52.472
And for many kids.
trust doesn't come easy.

256
00:15:53.473 --> 00:15:56.100
Trusting an adult with
something so personal...

257
00:15:56.893 --> 00:15:58.811
I can understand her silence.

258
00:16:01.647 --> 00:16:02.648
Hey. buddy.

259
